page-review
===========

A server-side Confluence 8.5 plugin that stores per-space GitLab repository settings.

Space administrators can configure:

* a full HTTPS GitLab repository URL (`https://host/group/project[.git]`);
* a target branch;
* an access token.

The token is encrypted with AES-256-GCM before it is stored in SAL plugin settings. It is never returned to the settings form. Leaving the token field empty preserves the existing token.

The settings form has a "Check connection" button that verifies the token can read the configured project and branch in GitLab without saving the form.

Documentation
-------------

The detailed wiki for engineers and AI agents starts at `docs/index.md`; the append-only change
log is `docs/log.md`.

Build and test
--------------

    mvn test
    atlas-package

Run a development Confluence instance with:

    atlas-run

The settings page is available from the administration menu of each space. The optional JVM property `pagereview.gitlab.allowed-hosts` restricts repository URLs to a comma-separated host allowlist.
